但吉姆太开心了。

1156
00:47:48.590 --> 00:47:51.490
Holly decides that this yoga guy is never going to call her.
霍莉认定那个瑜伽男永远不会给她打电话了。

1157
00:47:51.890 --> 00:47:53.670
And Michael says, you know what?
然后迈克尔说，你知道吗？

1158
00:47:53.730 --> 00:47:55.670
I'll buy the Counting Crows tickets from you.
我买下你手里的“数乌鸦”乐队门票。

1159
00:47:56.090 --> 00:47:57.510
And she's like, really?
她当时就想，真的吗？

1160
00:47:57.710 --> 00:48:00.250
Everybody thinks this is like going to lead to Michael
大家都以为这会引出迈克尔

1161
00:48:00.250 --> 00:48:01.830
offering to go with her?
主动提出陪她一起去？

1162
00:48:01.830 --> 00:48:04.090
I thought there were...
我以为有……

1163
00:48:04.090 --> 00:48:04.590
No.
没有。

1164
00:48:04.970 --> 00:48:06.870
Michael rips up the tickets.
迈克尔把票撕了。

1165
00:48:07.130 --> 00:48:08.370
Like gallantly.
表现得很大度。

1166
00:48:08.690 --> 00:48:10.290
Like he's saving the day.
就像他在拯救世界一样。

1167
00:48:10.530 --> 00:48:11.950
And she's confused.
她感到很困惑。

1168
00:48:12.450 --> 00:48:14.550
We got some mail from Emily G.
我们收到了艾米丽·G寄来的一封邮件。

1169
00:48:14.830 --> 00:48:15.130
Okay.
好的。

1170
00:48:15.230 --> 00:48:16.150
Here's what she said.
她是这么说的。

1171
00:48:16.390 --> 00:48:20.830
Having worked at several concert venues, I wanted to let you know that if you lose or
曾在几家音乐会场馆工作过，我想告诉你们，如果你们丢失或

1172
00:48:20.830 --> 00:48:25.550
damage your concert tickets, you can go to a venue's box office with your photo ID,
损坏了音乐会门票，可以带着带照片的身份证件去场馆的售票处，

1173
00:48:25.810 --> 00:48:27.750
and someone will reprint them for you.
会有人帮你们重新打印。

1174
00:48:28.070 --> 00:48:28.590
Oh.
噢。

1175
00:48:28.830 --> 00:48:31.490
She said, I hope Holly knew that was an option.
她说，希望霍莉当时知道还有这个选择。

1176
00:48:31.950 --> 00:48:33.150
Oh, that's good to know.
噢，这消息真有用。

1177
00:48:33.270 --> 00:48:33.770
Yeah.
是啊。

1178
00:48:34.150 --> 00:48:35.810
It didn't seem like Holly knew.
看起来霍莉当时并不知道。

1179
00:48:36.050 --> 00:48:36.350
No.
没。

1180
00:48:36.570 --> 00:48:37.450
I didn't know.
我也不知道。

1181
00:48:37.690 --> 00:48:38.750
Well, now we all know.
好吧，现在我们都知道了。

1182
00:48:38.750 --> 00:48:39.490
Now we all know.
现在我们都知道了。

1183
00:48:39.590 --> 00:48:40.350
Thank you, Emily.
谢谢你，艾米丽。

1184
00:48:40.550 --> 00:48:40.810
Yeah.
是啊。

1185
00:48:41.290 --> 00:48:48.070
In the end, Dunder Mifflin did not win the weight loss competition.
最终，邓德·米夫林公司没有赢得减肥比赛。

1186
00:48:48.650 --> 00:48:50.430
Stanley lost seven pounds.
斯坦利减掉了七磅。

1187
00:48:50.770 --> 00:48:51.070
Yeah.
是啊。

1188
00:48:51.270 --> 00:48:53.450
He says he's going to take off five days anyway.
他说反正他也要请五天假。

1189
00:48:53.750 --> 00:48:54.010
Yeah.
是啊。

1190
00:48:54.490 --> 00:48:55.890
And now it's week eight.
现在已经是第八周了。

1191
00:48:56.930 --> 00:49:00.530
Toby is on his fifth week in a hospital room in Costa Rica.
托比在哥斯达黎加的医院病房里待了五周了。

1192
00:49:00.790 --> 00:49:01.910
Oh, poor Toby.
噢，可怜的托比。

1193
00:49:01.910 --> 00:49:06.750
We guys remember Toby had his weird moment with Pam, so he moved to Costa Rica.
我们记得托比和帕姆之间有过那种尴尬时刻，所以他搬到了哥斯达黎加。

1194
00:49:07.010 --> 00:49:10.530
And on like his first day, or day, was it like day three?
结果就在他第一天，或者说，是第三天吧？

1195
00:49:10.730 --> 00:49:12.310
Day three, he went ziplining.
第三天，他去玩高空滑索。

1196
00:49:12.550 --> 00:49:13.870
And he broke his neck.
然后他摔断了脖子。

1197
00:49:14.110 --> 00:49:14.370
Yeah.
是啊。

1198
00:49:14.370 --> 00:49:16.430
He hasn't even been to the beach.
他甚至还没去过海滩呢。

1199
00:49:16.790 --> 00:49:19.770
Did you notice what was playing on the TV in the hospital room?
你注意到病房电视里在放什么了吗？

1200
00:49:19.970 --> 00:49:20.670
Yes, I did.
注意到了，我看到了。

1201
00:49:20.850 --> 00:49:23.970
It is the Hug It Out, Bitch episode of Entourage.
那是《明星伙伴》里“拥抱一下吧，碧池”那一集。

1202
00:49:24.610 --> 00:49:28.670
That is the episode of Entourage that Michael quotes in The Coup.
那就是迈克尔在《政变》那一集中引用的《明星伙伴》剧集。

1203
00:49:28.670 --> 00:49:33.370
Well, I have a little location breakdown for you about Toby's hospital room.
好吧，我为你准备了一份关于托比病房的拍摄地点细分。

1204
00:49:33.490 --> 00:49:34.110
Give it to me.
快告诉我。

1205
00:49:34.110 --> 00:49:36.330
It was also filmed at USC.
它也是在南加州大学拍摄的。

1206
00:49:36.750 --> 00:49:37.230
Oh!
噢！

1207
00:49:37.610 --> 00:49:37.890
Yeah.
没错。

1208
00:49:38.050 --> 00:49:42.890
While they were there filming Pam's art school, they used the USC television stage building.
当他们在那里拍摄帕姆的艺术学校时，他们使用了南加州大学的电视摄影棚大楼。

1209
00:49:43.210 --> 00:49:47.010
And USC asked if eight of their film students could intern and help that day.
南加州大学询问是否可以让八名电影系学生那天去实习帮忙。

1210
00:49:47.170 --> 00:49:49.090
They had interns in all of the different departments.
他们在各个不同的部门都安排了实习生。

1211
00:49:49.430 --> 00:49:51.950
And our crew said they did a phenomenal job.
我们的剧组人员说他们做得非常出色。

1212
00:49:52.170 --> 00:49:53.550
That is so cool.
太酷了。

1213
00:49:53.770 --> 00:49:54.110
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1214
00:49:54.110 --> 00:50:01.410
Before we go, I just want to give a shout out to whoever the guy is in the bed next to Toby.
在结束之前，我只想向托比隔壁床的那位仁兄致敬。

1215
00:50:01.910 --> 00:50:03.630
He was a background performer.
他是一位背景演员。

1216
00:50:03.850 --> 00:50:08.910
Angela, I tried so hard to figure out who this is because he is so funny.
安吉拉，我非常努力地想找出他是谁，因为他太搞笑了。

1217
00:50:09.290 --> 00:50:16.090
He just stares into the camera the whole time Toby is talking.
在托比说话的整个过程中，他一直盯着镜头看。

1218
00:50:16.310 --> 00:50:17.510
It is so good.
真是太棒了。

1219
00:50:17.530 --> 00:50:19.330
I watched it three times.
我看了三遍。

1220
00:50:19.330 --> 00:50:25.650
I was like, how is this guy doing such a great job with no words?
我当时就在想，这家伙是怎么做到一言不发却表现得这么好的？

1221
00:50:25.770 --> 00:50:26.830
I was so impressed.
我印象太深刻了。

1222
00:50:26.990 --> 00:50:28.330
We couldn't figure out who he was.
我们没能查出他是谁。

1223
00:50:28.450 --> 00:50:29.970
We reached out to several people.
我们联系了好几个人。

1224
00:50:30.230 --> 00:50:30.690
Yes.
是的。

1225
00:50:30.870 --> 00:50:32.870
And I checked everywhere you can check.
我查遍了所有能查的地方。

1226
00:50:33.050 --> 00:50:34.670
He is uncredited in the episode.
他在这一集中没有署名。

1227
00:50:35.630 --> 00:50:36.470
Phenomenal job.
表现太出色了。

1228
00:50:36.710 --> 00:50:37.770
Way to crush it.
干得漂亮。

1229
00:50:38.130 --> 00:50:41.010
That was weight loss part two.
那是《减肥》第二部分。

1230
00:50:41.550 --> 00:50:45.330
There's so many folks to thank for helping us get this episode out to you.
有太多人需要感谢，感谢他们帮助我们将这一集呈现给你们。

1231
00:50:45.330 --> 00:50:51.030
First of all, our crew that participated in the DVD commentary, Randy Cordray, Michael Gallenberg,
首先，参与DVD评论的剧组成员：兰迪·科德雷、迈克尔·加伦伯格、

1232
00:50:51.190 --> 00:50:56.650
Brian Whittle, Nick Carbone, Ben Patrick, Alicia Raycraft, Kelly Cantley, and Jake OuSt.
布莱恩·惠特尔、尼克·卡博内、本·帕特里克、艾丽西亚·雷克拉夫特、凯利·坎特利和杰克·奥斯特。

1233
00:50:57.170 --> 00:50:57.650
Amazing.
太棒了。

1234
00:50:58.090 --> 00:50:58.870
Best commentary.
最棒的评论。

1235
00:50:59.410 --> 00:51:02.530
Really such a good listen if you love behind-the-scenes information.
如果你喜欢幕后信息，这真的很值得一听。

1236
00:51:02.910 --> 00:51:05.890
And James O'Kerry for letting us bug you with questions.
还有詹姆斯·奥凯利，感谢你让我们用问题去烦你。

1237
00:51:06.430 --> 00:51:07.330
Yeah, we did.
没错，我们确实烦了。

1238
00:51:07.410 --> 00:51:08.250
We did bug him.
我们确实烦了他。

1239
00:51:08.390 --> 00:51:08.870
We did.
确实。

1240
00:51:09.010 --> 00:51:15.190
And Joya Balfour, oh my gosh, I'm so excited to share all of that NBC.com website stuff.
还有乔亚·巴尔福，天哪，我太兴奋能分享所有关于NBC.com网站的内容了。

1241
00:51:15.190 --> 00:51:18.110
And then Greg Daniels.
还有格雷格·丹尼尔斯。

1242
00:51:18.150 --> 00:51:18.430
Yes.
是的。

1243
00:51:18.710 --> 00:51:19.130
Thank you.
谢谢你。

1244
00:51:19.290 --> 00:51:21.950
And also Paul Feig for that audio clip.
还有保罗·费格提供的音频片段。

1245
00:51:22.130 --> 00:51:24.530
I promise not to bother you too much, Paul Feig.
我保证不会太打扰你，保罗·费格。

1246
00:51:24.950 --> 00:51:26.710
Well, we probably will.
好吧，我们可能会的。

1247
00:51:27.030 --> 00:51:27.630
I know.
我知道。

1248
00:51:27.730 --> 00:51:28.790
Why am I making that promise?
我为什么要做出那个承诺呢？

1249
00:51:28.950 --> 00:51:32.090
But we appreciate our cast and crew so much.
但我们非常感谢我们的演职人员。

1250
00:51:32.190 --> 00:51:33.930
We hope you enjoyed this one.
希望你们喜欢这一集。

1251
00:51:34.030 --> 00:51:35.970
And we are kicking off season five.
我们即将开启第五季。

1252
00:51:36.130 --> 00:51:37.450
We'll be back for more next week.
下周我们会带来更多精彩内容。

1253
00:51:37.570 --> 00:51:38.130
We sure will.
我们当然会。

